  "summary": "Denver Mayor Mike Johnston's office extended the city's Flock ALPR contract for five months at no cost, bypassing a City Council vote after the council unanimously rejected a longer extension in May. The new extension adds restrictions including a $100,000 penalty for any data shared with federal agencies, search-term limits excluding immigration and reproductive health queries, and required agreements barring other agencies from sharing data with ICE.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Extending Flock again without a vote undermines democratic oversight and public trust.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "Denver's new contract will include a requirement that Flock must pay $100,000 for any instance that data collected in the city is shared with federal agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "the Denver Police Department had revoked Loveland police's access to tracking data from Denver's Flock cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
